      about 20,000 tokens: 10 to 37 seconds here, once 62. KVMem keeps only four snapshots of
      the model’s state, all near the end of the last conversation. A <a href={`${repo}/blob/main/docs/measurements/2026-10-27-a-new-sessions-first-answer.md`}>patch
      that keeps one at the end of the system prompt</a> brought it to under a second, and my engine runs it since
      October 27: a new chat’s first word now comes in half a second to a second.
