    <h2 id="problems">What broke</h2>
    <ul class="problems">
      <li>NVIDIA driver 617.42, installed by the NVIDIA app on its own, crashed KVMem on 2 of 9 cache clears. On 591.74, none in 66. Automatic driver updates are off now.</li>
      <li>When the card filled, Windows moved part of the model into RAM, and it crawled at 10 tokens a second. The Sysmem Fallback setting below prevents that.</li>
      <li>CUDA graphs crashed it three times during speculative decoding. They are off.</li>
      <li>A tool result bigger than the window failed with HTTP 500. KVMem fixed it in <code>7e20823</code>, which I picked onto v0.16.</li>
      <li>OpenCode compacted too late once, and KVMem refused a 246,931-token prompt. Clank now gives OpenCode the window less 16,384 tokens.</li>
      <li>A busy desktop or a video on the same card halves the speed.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="settings">The settings</h2>
